Creative Commons Legal Code

CC0 1.0 Universal

CREATIVE COMMONS CORPORATION IS NOT A LAW FIRM, AND DOES NOT PROVIDE
LEGAL SERVICES. DISTRIBUTION OF THIS DOCUMENT DOES NOT CREATE AN
ATTORNEY-CLIENT RELIEN. CREATIVE COMMONS MAKES NO WARRANTY REGARDING
THE USE OF THIS DOCUMENT AND DEDICATES IT TO THE PUBLIC DOMAIN.


Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically grant
to creators (authors and inventors) exclusive rights in the works they
create. Some of those rights (the "copyright" in written works, for
example) are available for others to use after a certain period. This
document (the "CC0 Legal Document") describes a way for creators to give
up all of those rights and dedicate their works to the public domain.

The creator of a work (a "creator") may wish to give up all rights in
it. To the extent this is legally possible, the creator of this work
hereby waives all rights in the work, and asks that the public not hold
the creator responsible for any use of the work, while assuring the
public that the work will not be subject to any claim of ownership by
the creator.

For the full text of the CC0 1.0 Universal legal code, please see:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
